# Game car 2, second sheet. PDF page 10, block B.
# Written like a MAME netlist: chips by location, then each wire as the pins it joins.
# tools/generate_netlist.py names the Verilog wires from the pins: docs/NET_NAMES.md.
chip L6 7432
chip L8 7404
chip J8 74112
chip J7 7420
chip J5 74193
chip H5 74192   # preset 2: pin 1 alone on B999, which crosses the ground bus of 15/10/9 without a dot (fixed 2026-11-15, DR-1A 10K agrees)
chip K7 7432
chip L7 7420   # pin 9 was traced as 11, which a 7420 does not have; the twin E3.8 on sheet 10 uses 9
# Drawing labels the lower inputs 10/11 rather than standard 9/10; preserve it.
chip K6 74193
chip J6 74193   # preset 1: pin 15 alone on B999; 1/10/9 on the ground bus (fixed 2026-11-15, DR-1A 10H agrees)
prom H6 82S129 91
chip H8 7404
chip Q3 7427
chip R4 7411
# Fixed 2026-11-05: pin 2 meets the inverter output at G9.12, not its input. Death Race B/D agree.
chip H7 7410
chip H9 7421
chip H10 7411
chip G11 7432
chip H11 7421
chip G10 74112
chip G9 74112
chip F4 7408
chip G8 74112
chip K8 7486
chip C10 7408

# Wires: drawing label, then every pin it joins on this sheet. BOARD marks a
# wire that rtl/deathrac_board.v drives or reads. GND/VCC are tied pins, OPEN a
# visibly floating input, NC a drawn output stub that goes nowhere.
net BEGA L6.3 L8.3 J7.13
net 5TCBG L6.1 L6.5
net 1ACT3 L6.2
net BEGB L6.6 J8.2 J8.3 J7.4 J7.12
net 5AECC L6.4
net 5BEGA L8.4 J7.5
net 2LQ07 J8.1 J8.13 G10.1 G10.13 G9.1
net B999 J8.4 J8.15 J5.10 J5.9 H5.1 J6.15 G10.4 G10.15 G10.10 G10.14 G9.10 G8.4 G8.15 G8.10 G8.14 BOARD
net BEC1 J8.5 J7.9
net 5BEC1 J8.6 J7.1
net 6BQED J7.6 J5.4
net 1LQ07 J7.2 J7.10 L7.2 L7.12
net 6BQEU J7.8 J5.5
net 5APRS J5.11 H5.11 K6.11 J6.11
net GND J5.14 J5.15 J5.1 H5.14 H5.15 H5.10 H5.9 K6.14 K6.15 K6.1 K6.10 K6.9 J6.14 J6.1 J6.10 J6.9
net NC J5.3 H5.13 H5.12 J6.13 J6.12 G9.6 G9.7 G8.7
